    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0288" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3238</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Egan</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-06T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.05 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>439. To-day at 5 o’clock the Foreign Minister brought me the following: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I authorize you to communicate to your Government that in the opinion of
                            the Danish Government the position of Denmark both actually and formally
                            is so different from that of the United States <pb facs="0289" n="117"
                                xml:id="pg117"/> that it is not possible to draw an analogy from the
                            one to the other, and further that the three northern governments are in
                            consultation with one another at Stockholm in order to fix on a basis of
                            international law the attitude to be taken by them on account of the new
                            German regulations.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
